          "type": "concept",
          "title": "Alexander's Successors and the Birth of Ptolemaic Egypt",
          "content": "When Alexander the Great died in Babylon in 323 BCE, his vast empire was divided among his generals, the so-called Diadochi or \"Successors.\" Ptolemy son of Lagos, one of Alexander's closest companions and bodyguards, seized Egypt as his prize. He stole Alexander's corpse en route to Macedonia and entombed it in Alexandria, anchoring his legitimacy to the conqueror's body. By 305 BCE, Ptolemy declared himself king, founding the Ptolemaic dynasty that would rule Egypt for 275 years until Cleopatra's death. The Ptolemies governed as Greek-speaking foreigners ruling an ancient Egyptian population, layering Hellenistic kingship onto the immense apparatus of pharaonic tradition.",
          "visual": {
            "type": "diagram",
            "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><rect width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" font-size=\"36\" fill=\"#ffd700\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">From Alexander to the Ptolemies</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" font-size=\"24\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">How a Macedonian Dynasty Took Egypt</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"170\" width=\"940\" height=\"130\" fill=\"#16213e\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#6366f1\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">323 BCE: Alexander Dies in Babylon</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"250\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Empire stretches from Greece to India</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"280\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">No clear heir; generals carve up the territories</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"320\" width=\"940\" height=\"130\" fill=\"#16213e\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"360\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">322 BCE: Ptolemy Seizes Egypt and the Body</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"400\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Hijacks Alexander's funeral cortege to Memphis</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"430\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Possession of the corpse equals legitimacy</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"470\" width=\"940\" height=\"130\" fill=\"#16213e\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"510\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#10b981\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">305 BCE: Ptolemy I Soter Crowned King</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"550\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Adopts pharaonic titles alongside Greek basileus</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"580\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Founds the dynasty that will rule until 30 BCE</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"620\" width=\"940\" height=\"130\" fill=\"#16213e\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">Three Successor Kingdoms Form</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"700\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Antigonids in Macedonia, Seleucids in Asia</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"730\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Ptolemies in Egypt - the wealthiest of the three</text><rect x=\"80\" y=\"770\" width=\"940\" height=\"160\" fill=\"#16213e\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"2\" rx=\"10\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"810\" font-size=\"26\" fill=\"#ec4899\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">The Ptolemaic Formula</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"850\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Greek court, Greek army, Greek language at top</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"880\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Egyptian temples, priesthood, taxation below</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"910\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#ffffff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Two parallel systems held together by the throne</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"980\" font-size=\"22\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-style=\"italic\">A Macedonian queen would become Egypt's most famous pharaoh</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1020\" font-size=\"18\" fill=\"#9ca3af\" text-anchor=\"middle\">275 years of foreign dynasty culminating in Cleopatra VII</text></svg>",
            "caption": "Ptolemy I founded the dynasty in 305 BCE by fusing Greek kingship with Egyptian tradition."
          }
