        type: "intro",
        title: "Inside the Bruchion Palace",
        content: "The Ptolemaic royal palace was not a single building but an entire district — the Bruchion — occupying perhaps a quarter of Alexandria. Greek geographer Strabo, who walked through it in 25 BCE just a few years after Cleopatra's death, described an architectural cascade descending toward the harbor: separate palaces for each successive Ptolemy, the Mouseion, the Sema mausoleum housing Alexander the Great's body, the theater, the Timonium where Antony brooded after Actium, and groves of trees and porticoes connecting them. Within this district lived perhaps 10,000 people: royal family members, ministers, eunuchs, tutors, philosophers, physicians, Macedonian Companions descended from Alexander's officers, Egyptian priests, scribes, dancers, cooks, and slaves.\n\nThe Alexandrian court was the most sophisticated political ecosystem in the ancient Mediterranean — and the most lethal. The Ptolemies practiced sibling marriage to keep dynastic power concentrated, and the resulting families were saturated with murder. Cleopatra's father killed her older sister Berenice IV. Cleopatra herself either killed or arranged the deaths of her brother-husbands Ptolemy XIII and Ptolemy XIV and her sister Arsinoe IV. The palace was a place where children learned to negotiate, dissemble, and survive before they could read.\n\nAt the center of palace politics stood a small group of senior advisers — the philoi (Friends) of the king. These were not blood relatives. They were trained operators: eunuchs who ran the regency during minorities, tutors who controlled the heir's education, finance ministers who knew where every drachma flowed. This lesson dissects who actually held power inside the palace walls during Cleopatra's reign, how court factions operated, and how the queen navigated a household where political miscalculation meant death.",
        visual: {
          type: "diagram",
          svg: `<svg viewBox="0 0 1100 1100" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><rect width="1100" height="1100" fill="#1a1a2e"/><text x="550" y="50" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="28" font-weight="bold">The Bruchion Palace District</text><text x="550" y="90" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="18">Royal Quarter, Alexandria — c. 40 BCE</text><rect x="100" y="130" width="900" height="400" fill="none" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="3"/><text x="550" y="160" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="16">Bruchion District — ~25% of city area</text><rect x="130" y="180" width="160" height="100" fill="#6366f1" opacity="0.3" stroke="#6366f1" stroke-width="2"/><text x="210" y="220" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Cleopatra's</text><text x="210" y="240" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Palace</text><rect x="310" y="180" width="160" height="100" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.3" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="390" y="220" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Mouseion +</text><text x="390" y="240" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Library</text><rect x="490" y="180" width="160" height="100" fill="#f59e0b" opacity="0.3" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="2"/><text x="570" y="220" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Sema</text><text x="570" y="240" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">(Alexander's tomb)</text><rect x="670" y="180" width="160" height="100" fill="#ec4899" opacity="0.3" stroke="#ec4899" stroke-width="2"/><text x="750" y="220" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Theater</text><text x="750" y="245" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Stadium</text><rect x="850" y="180" width="140" height="100" fill="#8b5cf6" opacity="0.3" stroke="#8b5cf6" stroke-width="2"/><text x="920" y="220" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="13">Timonium</text><text x="920" y="245" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="13">(Antony's)</text><rect x="130" y="310" width="220" height="100" fill="#0ea5e9" opacity="0.3" stroke="#0ea5e9" stroke-width="2"/><text x="240" y="350" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Earlier Ptolemy</text><text x="240" y="375" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Palaces (5+)</text><rect x="370" y="310" width="280" height="100" fill="#ef4444" opacity="0.3" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2"/><text x="510" y="350" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Inner Harbor (Royal)</text><text x="510" y="375" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Lochias Promontory</text><rect x="670" y="310" width="320" height="100" fill="#10b981" opacity="0.2" stroke="#10b981" stroke-width="2"/><text x="830" y="350" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Palace Gardens + Groves</text><text x="830" y="375" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Porticoes connecting buildings</text><text x="550" y="460" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="16">Population: ~10,000 within palace district</text><text x="550" y="490" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">Royal family, ministers, eunuchs, tutors, scholars,</text><text x="550" y="515" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="14">physicians, dancers, cooks, guards, slaves</text><line x1="100" y1="570" x2="1000" y2="570" stroke="#ffd700" stroke-width="2"/><text x="550" y="610" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="22" font-weight="bold">A Lethal Ecosystem</text><text x="550" y="660" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="16">Ptolemy XII killed daughter Berenice IV (55 BCE)</text><text x="550" y="690" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="16">Cleopatra arranged death of Ptolemy XIII (47 BCE)</text><text x="550" y="720" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="16">Cleopatra poisoned Ptolemy XIV (44 BCE)</text><text x="550" y="750" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ef4444" font-size="16">Cleopatra arranged murder of Arsinoe IV (41 BCE)</text><text x="550" y="800" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffd700" font-size="18" font-weight="bold">5 dead siblings in 14 years</text><text x="550" y="860" text-anchor="middle" fill="#ffffff" font-size="16">Palace politics ran on three currencies:</text><text x="550" y="900" text-anchor="middle" fill="#6366f1" font-size="18">EUNUCHS — TUTORS — TREASURY</text><text x="550" y="970" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="14">Strabo walked this district in 25 BCE and described it</text><text x="550" y="1000" text-anchor="middle" fill="#888" font-size="14">"the most beautiful royal residences of the world"</text></svg>`,
          caption: "The Bruchion district: cascading palaces, Mouseion, Alexander's tomb, theaters — a city within a city of 10,000 souls."
        }
